Sourcing: ${source_priorities}. Evidence norms: a statement about an arrangement needs a source with a pinpoint (page, article, paragraph, line); describe practice and attribute judgements; the legal status of a use is a question for the referral list, not a finding; numbers verbatim with their unit. Recency: ${period}. Local project material (${local_corpus}) is first-hand team evidence and should be ingested; AI-generated notes are never evidence; summaries and wiki pages are pointers to originals. Cite every claim as [[note-id|pinpoint]] so the deliverable can be converted to ${citation_style} footnotes. PLACE FOCUS: tie every arrangement to named places or points (springs, wells, intakes, weirs, dams, canal reaches, river reaches, lakes, extraction stretches, villages) with the administrative hierarchy, the hydrological location and coordinates where sourced; prefer site case studies and local news over generic commentary. Search in ${languages}; local terms to search for: ${local_terms}. Out of scope: ${out_of_scope}.
